(=== UNIT 4: RAPID PROTOTYPING & USER EXPERIENCE \(UX\) DESIGN ===) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.1 Prototyping Philosophy and Rapid Learning Loops) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A prototype is a tangible, testable manifestation of an idea built to answer specific) Tj
T*
(design questions and test critical hypotheses rapidly:) Tj
T*
(* 'Build to Think, Think to Build': Prototypes are not finished miniature products;) Tj
T*
(they are learning instruments. Physical construction exposes unexpected friction) Tj
T*
(points that remain hidden in theoretical diagrams.) Tj
T*
(* Fail Fast, Learn Faster: Low-cost rapid prototyping minimizes the sunk-cost) Tj
T*
(fallacy. Discovering fatal flaws during day 2 of prototyping costs $10; discovering) Tj
T*
(them after software launch costs millions.) Tj
T*
(* The Fidelity Spectrum:) Tj
T*
(- Low-Fidelity \(Lo-Fi\): Fast, cheap, disposable artifacts \(paper sketches, cardboard) Tj
T*
(models, wireframes\). Used early to validate concepts, user flows, and information) Tj
T*
(hierarchy.) Tj
T*
(- High-Fidelity \(Hi-Fi\): Polished, interactive digital mockups or 3D-printed physical) Tj
T*
(assemblies with realistic visual aesthetics, fonts, and functional micro-interactions.) Tj
T*
(Used late to validate usability, latency, and detailed ergonomics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.2 Paper Prototyping and Storyboarding for Software) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Paper Prototyping: Hand-drawn paper screens, pop-up dialog cutouts, and sticky-note) Tj
T*
(dropdowns simulating software mobile or web interfaces. One designer acts as the) Tj
T*
('Human Computer', manipulating paper elements in real-time as the test user taps) Tj
T*
(paper buttons.) Tj
T*
(* Storyboarding: Sequential visual narrative depicting a user journey before, during,) Tj
T*
(and after interacting with a product. Contextualizes the emotional trigger, user) Tj
T*
(friction, and ultimate value delivery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.3 Digital Wireframing and Information Architecture) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Information Architecture \(IA\): Structural blueprint of how information is) Tj
T*
(categorized, labeled, and navigated across digital software systems.) Tj
T*
(* Wireframing: Grayscale, visual representations of interface layouts focusing on) Tj
T*
(structural hierarchy, visual balance, and functionality without color or graphic) Tj
T*
(distractions.) Tj
T*
(* Wireframe Fidelity Levels: Low-fidelity \(rough block layout\), Mid-fidelity) Tj
T*
ET

