(>> 4.4 The Minimum Viable Product \(MVP\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Coined by Frank Robinson and popularized by Eric Ries \(The Lean Startup\), an MVP is the) Tj
T*
(simplest version of a new product that allows a team to collect the maximum amount of) Tj
T*
(validated learning about customers with the least engineering effort:) Tj
T*
(* MVP Types:) Tj
T*
(- Wizard of Oz MVP: The front-end appears automated and sophisticated, but behind the) Tj
T*
(scenes, humans perform all algorithmic tasks manually \(e.g., Zappos originally) Tj
T*
(photographed shoes in retail stores and mailed them manually when orders arrived\).) Tj
T*
(- Concierge MVP: Providing services entirely manually and transparently to high-value) Tj
T*
(pilot customers before writing a single line of software.) Tj
T*
(- Piecemeal MVP: Combining existing off-the-shelf software tools \(e.g. Google Forms +) Tj
T*
(Zapier + Google Sheets\) to validate workflows without custom code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 1: The PalmPilot Wooden Block Prototype]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: In 1995, Jeff Hawkins was designing the PalmPilot PDA. His engineering) Tj
T*
(team debated screen sizes, stylus interactions, and whether users would actually carry) Tj
T*
(an electronic organizer in their pockets.) Tj
T*
(Rapid Prototyping Intervention:) Tj
T*
(Lo-Fi Prototype: Hawkins carved a simple piece of wood to the exact proposed PalmPilot) Tj
T*
(dimensions and whittled a short wooden peg to act as a stylus.) Tj
T*
(In-Context Testing: For months, Hawkins carried this wooden block in his shirt pocket.) Tj
T*
(In meetings, he pulled it out, tapped on drawn paper buttons, and evaluated whether the) Tj
T*
(form factor felt natural or annoying.) Tj
T*
(Learnings & Product Impact: He discovered that instant single-tap calendar and memo) Tj
T*
(retrieval was 100x more important than full desktop syncing, resulting in the) Tj
T*
(streamlined PalmPilot interface that dominated the market.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 2: Paper Prototyping a Hospital Patient Check-in Kiosk]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A software team was tasked with building automated self-service) Tj
T*
(touchscreen check-in kiosks for a public hospital to reduce admissions queue wait times) Tj
T*
(from 45 minutes to 5 minutes.) Tj
T*
ET

