(Paper Prototyping Session:) Tj
T*
(Lo-Fi Artifacts: Cardboard box cut to kiosk dimensions, with hand-drawn paper screens) Tj
T*
(slipped into a clear acrylic sleeve. Paper cards simulated health insurance cards and) Tj
T*
(driver's licenses.) Tj
T*
(Human Computer Role: A developer sat behind the cardboard box, swapping paper screens) Tj
T*
(when test patients tapped buttons.) Tj
T*
(Critical Usability Discoveries in 2 Hours:) Tj
T*
(- Elderly patients tapped the paper screen too forcefully, expecting physical button) Tj
T*
(depression.) Tj
T*
(- Users were confused by medical jargon \('Ailment Taxonomy'\); terminology was simplified) Tj
T*
(to 'Where does it hurt?'.) Tj
T*
(- Barcode scanners placed at the bottom were blocked by wheelchairs; redesigned to an) Tj
T*
(accessible 45-degree angled shelf.) Tj
T*
(Outcome: Fixed 14 fundamental UI and ergonomic defects on day 1 before writing any) Tj
T*
(front-end software code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
