T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 3: Dropbox Explainer Video as a Wizard-of-Oz MVP]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: In 2007, Drew Houston conceived Dropbox: seamless cloud file) Tj
T*
(synchronization across diverse operating systems. Building the distributed file) Tj
T*
(synchronization architecture required millions of dollars and deep systems engineering.) Tj
T*
(Lean MVP Execution:) Tj
T*
(The MVP was NOT software. It was a simple 3-minute screen-recorded video demonstration) Tj
T*
(narrated by Drew Houston showing how the proposed desktop folder would seamlessly sync) Tj
T*
(files across Macs and PCs.) Tj
T*
(Houston posted the video to Hacker News and Digg with a simple email waitlist capture) Tj
T*
(form.) Tj
T*
(Measurable Results: In 24 hours, the beta waiting list jumped from 5,000 to 75,000) Tj
T*
(sign-ups, providing incontrovertible market validation that secured venture funding) Tj
T*
(before complex server infrastructure was constructed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 4: Storyboarding an Emergency Blood Donation Mobile App]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A student team built an emergency blood donor matching app, but) Tj
T*
(hospital blood banks reported donor response rates were under 5%.) Tj
T*
(Storyboarding the Complete Human Journey \(6 Panels\):) Tj
T*
(Panel 1 \(Trigger\): ICU doctor enters urgent need for O-negative blood for accident) Tj
T*
(victim.) Tj
T*
